-names>SW</given-names></name><name><surname>Kawashima</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Mohandas</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Regulation of CD44-protein 4.1 interaction by Ca2+ and calmodulin. Implications for modulation of CD44-ankyrin interaction</article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><year>1997</year><volume>272</volume><fpage>30322</fpage><lpage>30328</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9374519</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1074/jbc.272.48.30322</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hung</surname><given-names>LY</given-names></name><name><surname>Tang</surname><given-names>CJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Tang</surname><given-names>TK</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Protein 4.1 R-135 interacts with a novel centrosomal protein (CPAP) which is associated with the &#x003b3;-tubulin complex</article-title><source>Mol Cell Biol</source><year>2000</year><volume>20</volume><fpage>7813</fpage><lpage>7825</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11003675</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1128/MCB.20.20.7813-7825.2000</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Correas</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Avila</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Erythrocyte protein 4.1 associates with tubulin</article-title><source>Biochem J</source><year>1988</year><volume>255</volume><fpage>217</fpage><lpage>221</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3196314</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Perez-Ferreiro</surname><given-names>CM</given-names></name><name><surname>Luque</surname><given-names>CM</given-names></name><name><surname>Correas</surname><given-names>I</given-n